                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d2eb8c1b-0c2a-4eb3-a23b-5826ee318efd",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5a0894a-b808-3c6d-8aea-ff96fc082b67",
                        "source_sense_id": "4a948f83-1033-3768-b21d-010ee735d134",
                        "source_sense_description": "chinesische Provinz im Osten der Volksrepublik China",
                        "target_lang_word": "Henan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Henan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "13f74fc4-2dd6-3444-b6e6-de559fc84097",
                                        "entry_id": "2fa557dc-24f3-3f2e-a55b-f78069da72b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A province of China. Capital: Zhengzhou."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0132bd3-5435-419f-a63b-cd511c0ab0e0",
                                                "sense_id": "13f74fc4-2dd6-3444-b6e6-de559fc84097",
                                                "text": "Heavy rainfall inundated streets and caused major rivers to burst their banks in the central province of Henan on Tuesday.[…]\nHenan is a particularly populous province and a major transport hub. It is also a key base for industry and agriculture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6545bec-e852-4b59-a968-bd403a1aa28a",
                                                "sense_id": "13f74fc4-2dd6-3444-b6e6-de559fc84097",
                                                "text": "Security forces attacked as many as a thousand protesters who were trying to withdraw their money from four rural banks in Henan Province this weekend."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da68521d-deb6-4b72-a586-13ee142b333f",
                                                "sense_id": "13f74fc4-2dd6-3444-b6e6-de559fc84097",
                                                "text": "Gao moved to New York in 2009 after years of harassment by Chinese officials believed to be nursing grudges after she exposed a cover-up of the true extent of the AIDS epidemic in central Henan province.[…]\nExperts estimate at least one million farmers in Henan alone contracted HIV/AIDS in the blood trade."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f48eb95-97ce-3137-8d53-8ea0c547ae8b",
                                        "entry_id": "2fa557dc-24f3-3f2e-a55b-f78069da72b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Mongol autonomous county in the Tibetan autonomous prefecture of Huangnan prefecture, Qinghai Province, China. Official name: Henan Mongol Autonomous County."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e14a0c3-f57d-4b23-b2df-2ab410cc938a",
                                                "sense_id": "0f48eb95-97ce-3137-8d53-8ea0c547ae8b",
                                                "text": "The very next day, Tenzin Nyima was transferred to a prison in Henan Mongolian Autonomous County for six days of questioning.[…]\nOnce in Henan, Tenzin Nyima quickly came to know that Lodroe and Rigdrol, the monks who had helped with the flags, had also been seized."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b812f7b6-702f-4370-992d-efa4482adad5",
                                                "sense_id": "0f48eb95-97ce-3137-8d53-8ea0c547ae8b",
                                                "text": "HENAN MONGOL AUTONOMOUS COUNTY (SOGWO)[…]\nIn Henan County, 325km south of Xining, 90 percent of its 27,000 people are Mongolian.[…]\nThere is a bus to Henan that leaves Xining at 07:30 everyday.^([sic])"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61b5871c-2537-4b08-8989-93fda98d7600",
                                                "sense_id": "0f48eb95-97ce-3137-8d53-8ea0c547ae8b",
                                                "text": "Located in the southeast of China’s Qinghai (Kökenuur) province, Henan Mongol Autonomous County has an area of 7,000 square kilometers (2,700 square miles). Henan lies on the eastern edge of the Tibetan plateau at an altitude mostly over 3,500 meters (11,500 feet) and shares the plateau’s strong sunlight, cool summers, and extremely unpredictable weather."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06c2da94-27a8-4b30-b5c7-0b504dbcc1a1",
                                                "sense_id": "0f48eb95-97ce-3137-8d53-8ea0c547ae8b",
                                                "text": "The Henan Mongol autonomous county (xian) is inhabited by Tsoros Mongols, and there are Ööld Mongols in the Huzhu autonomous county."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "02d56a11-b190-3ca8-8892-f54e03b9d6fd",
                                        "entry_id": "2fa557dc-24f3-3f2e-a55b-f78069da72b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An island and former district, now part of Haizhu District south of the old urban core of Guangzhou, Guangdong, China."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b40f9081-196c-41e8-b9a0-350efc2c6844",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5a0894a-b808-3c6d-8aea-ff96fc082b67",
                        "source_sense_id": "4a948f83-1033-3768-b21d-010ee735d134",
                        "source_sense_description": "chinesische Provinz im Osten der Volksrepublik China",
                        "target_lang_word": "Honan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Honan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                        "entry_id": "af713a81-8103-3677-8608-6920dece37eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of Henan, in its various senses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a7e0e61-a0fe-4127-8d83-decddf77f354",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "THe fifth Province of Honan, hath receiv'd its Name from the Situation of the place, for Honan ſignifies The South ſide of a River ; for it lies on the South Shore of the Yellow River, which flowing from Eaſt to Weſt, ſeparates it from the Province of Xanſi and Peking, though to the Eaſt, toward the ſide of Peking it hath ſome Towns."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18cf3560-6323-4b80-973e-fbc0016744b0",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "The Province of Honan, by the Chineſes thought to lie in the middle of the World, becauſe it lies in the midſt of China ; it is divided into nine Territories or Countries, having one hundred and eight Cities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "480bc2d4-cf45-44da-ae1e-c0a9bfda4e0a",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "The Province of Honan lies on both ſides the River Hoang, and (according to the Opinion of the Inhabitants) in the Centre of the Terreſtrial Globe ; abounding with Rivulets and all manner of Delights, the Air being very Temperate, and the Soil exceeding fruitful : Inſomuch that it is reputed a kind of Paradiſe by the Chineſes, and upon that Account it was heretofore choſen at ſeveral times, for the Seat of the Imperial Court : It is divided into nine Parts, whoſe chief Towns are Hoaiking ; Honan ; Caifung, the Capital City ; Changto ; Queite ; Guihoei ; Juning ; and Nanyang ; a hundred more principal Cities ſtand in this Province."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4a6bc13-4501-4a2f-aaad-7dcdc90874a4",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "\"THE MIDDLE KINGDOM\" was one of the earliest names given by the Chinese to designate the land which they inhabited. The use of this name with reference to China dates from the period of the Chow dynasty, about B.C. 1150. The Imperial family gave the name to its own state Honan, because it was central to all the other states. As the empire grew the name remained and for many centuries this was one of the titles given by the natives to the entire territory ruled by their Emperor. China was believed to be central to all other nations, Honan was central in China, and it was easy to conclude that the Chinese were the most important people of the world. During the eventful millenniums of China's chequered history, rulers and statesmen deemed it wise no fewer than seventeen times to change the situation of the nation's capital. It says something for the importance of Honan that seven times out of the seventeen the honour of having one of its cities chosen as capital feel to this province."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9ef26b4-db96-4743-b410-f25738eecdbb",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "Ju is an imperial ware of the Sung Dynasty, that takes its name from the district in Honan where it was first developed; the kiln site has not yet been firmly identified. The ware is generally believed to have been made for the Northern Sung court only from A.D. 1107 to 1127, the latter date coinciding with the enforced withdrawal of the court to Hang-chou in the south, as the result of the Chin Tartar invasion from the north."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "077267f2-2804-4751-8cdf-729c92f1f348",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "Perhaps the most important monument of Chinese Buddhist sculpture in the Rietberg collection, this stele was acquired by Baron von der Heydt before 1924, after having been in the possession of C.T. Loo, Paris. It is most likely the work of a metropolitan sculptor's atelier located in the vicinity of present Cheng-chou in Honan Province."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "542c7853-977d-4dc6-a891-93396e4747e2",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "More recently, a Ch’u tomb at Hsi-ch’uan, Honan Province, dated to the Spring and Autumn period, has yielded several bronze vessels with decoration that suggests to the authors of the archaeological report that they might have been cast by the lost-wax method (see WW, no. 10 [1980]: 21–26, especially p. 23, pls. 1–2)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "248e47de-5bd4-467a-be6c-03ce2cd12c4c",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "Wang, a native of Honan Province, told government officials he had taken off from an airfield in Taishan, an island 75 miles southeast of Shanghai on the east coast of mainland China.\n. . .\nAs the news of the freedom flight hit the streets of Taiwan, rounds of firecrackers could be heard exploding throughout the cities, and residents put up posters to both announce the news and express their welcome for the young pilot from Honan Province."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3155549d-30ad-4cba-a611-df9c0db9cdd2",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "It was about this time that Emperor Ai-tsung, who had fled Kai-feng in hopes of mounting a counteroffensive, committed suicide in Tsʻai-chou, Honan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d94901a-de9c-4911-b66c-ed85e281e08c",
                                                "sense_id": "cc5c07c0-bf3f-3d29-a742-e7d1d059c176",
                                                "text": "The central territory of the Shang realm lay in north-western Honan, alongside the Shansi Mountains and extending into the plains. It was a peasant civilization with towns. The Shang state had its centre in northern Honan, north of the Yellow river."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
